WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.100
-Welcome, welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.667
You're here.
Thank you for being here.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.434
Welcome. Welcome.

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:08.934
Did you read this today?

00:00:08.934 --> 00:00:10.200
I thought this was
very interesting.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.133
I saw that Costco is now
offering one-ounce gold bars

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.868
for $2,000.

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:19.200
And they're selling out.
Gold bars.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.934
Yeah, even weirder,
at Kay Jewelers,

00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:22.467
they're giving out
free cheese samples.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.334
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:25.634
So if you're keeping track,

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:28.234
you can buy gold bars at Costco
no problem,

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.067
but CVS still keeps
their deodorant

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.334
locked behind bulletproof glass.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:34.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.801
"You want 24-hour protection?

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:40.000
I got to call my manager.
Hold on."

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.467
Some more business news --

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.767
Uber just announced
that you can now have drivers

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:45.400
deliver your return packages

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.501
to the post office,
FedEx, or UPS.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:49.534
That makes sense.

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:51.100
At night,
they drive drunk people,

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.100
and in the morning,
they drive the stuff

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.601
that the drunk people order.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.701
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.701 --> 00:00:58.567
Perfect.
-Circle of life.

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:03.300
-♪ The circle of life ♪

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.000
Well, big news from Washington.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.868
Oh, my goodness.
Hey, quick show of hands.

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.601
Does anybody here want
to be Speaker of the House?

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:12.067
Okay.
Everybody is talking about this.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:15.133
Kevin McCarthy
was ousted from his job,

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.667
and now there's no
Speaker of the House.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:20.300
But next week, a vote
will be held to replace him.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.267
And a lot of people
are calling it a thankless job

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.667
that's borderline impossible.

00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:25.100
Yeah, it's not much fun.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.400
And most Republicans say
that they're not interested.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:30.300
They actually are using
special excuse generators

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:31.601
to get out of it.

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.000
I'll show you what I mean.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.901
For instance,
when Congressman Mike Rodgers

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.467
was asked to run for speaker,

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:38.501
the generator told him to say...

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.567
-Oh.
-Do you see how it works?

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.067
They're just
giving them excuses.

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:49.767
-That was random?
-Let me show you. Random.

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:52.701
Next up, when Congressman
Jack Bergman was asked,

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:53.767
he said...

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.601
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:04.267
I mean, they're helping --
They want a way out of this.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.634
So they use
the excuse generator.

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:06.968
Check this out.

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:09.534
When Congressman Michael Guest
was asked, he said...

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.601
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:19.968
-Wow.
-That's his job.

00:02:19.968 --> 00:02:21.000
Here's another one.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.968
When Congressman
Mark Amodei was asked,

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.267
he said...

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:31.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:32.968
That's impossible.
-Wow.

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:34.400
-They don't make them.
-That's random.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:36.667
-He's on the hunt.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:37.801
-You got to be safe.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:39.167
-Got to be safe.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:41.100
And next up, when Congressman
Austin Scott was asked,

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:42.434
he said...

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:50.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.934
That's what he tells women
in bars.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.400
-At bars.
-I don't know. Here's another.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.400
When Congressman Chuck Edwards
was asked, he said...

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:04.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:08.100
That's impossible.
That's hard to do.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.868
And finally, when Congressman
John Carter was asked,

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.200
he said...

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:19.934
So these are just
some of the excuses.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:21.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.901
Meanwhile,
with Kevin McCarthy out,

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:28.567
North Carolina congressman
Patrick McHenry

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.667
will serve
as the interim speaker.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:33.534
Yeah, Kevin McCarthy
and Patrick McHenry,

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:36.000
they have similar names,
so it's a little confusing.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:38.167
Here, let me
break it down for you.

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:40.167
[ Rhythmic tapping ]

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:44.300
Kevin McCarthy.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.400
Patrick McHenry.

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:48.400
Kevin McCarthy.

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.300
Patrick McHenry.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.234
McHenry. McCarthy.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:54.467
McHenry. McCarthy.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:56.367
Two men.

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:58.400
Same party.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.267
McCarthy. McGarvey.
McCollum. McCaul.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:06.367
McCarthy. McCarthy.
McCartney. McGraw.

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:08.367
McCarthy. McGovern.
McCormick. McBath.

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.467
McClellan. Mick Jagger.
McCheese. Back to Pat.

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.534
McCarthy. McGovern.
McLovin. McRib.

00:04:12.534 --> 00:04:14.467
Matthew McConaughey.
Now back to Mick.

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:16.501
Kevin and Kevin
and Kevin and Matt.

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.534
Matt ousted Kevin,
and now we have Pat.

00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:20.534
Patrick and Patty
and Patrick and Pat.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.501
Kevin and Kevin James
meme format.

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:24.467
Pat McHenry after him.

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.667
Pat, Pat, Kev, Kev,
Matt, Matt, Jim.

00:04:26.667 --> 00:04:28.934
I just hope that was --

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:30.834
I just hope that was helpful.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.868
Are we okay?
Was that helpful?

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:42.234
I hope that was helpful, yeah.

00:04:42.234 --> 00:04:44.367
That's right,
after McCarthy was voted out,

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:47.567
McHenry got to bang the gavel
for the first time as speaker.

00:04:47.567 --> 00:04:49.200
Let's see how that went.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:50.934
-The chair declares
the House in recess,

00:04:50.934 --> 00:04:52.834
subject to the call
of the chair.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:55.167
[ Sputters ]

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.968
[ Laughs ]

00:04:59.968 --> 00:05:01.734
Trouble at home, Pat?

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:04.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:07.467
Wow. That's pretty aggressive
with the gavel there.

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:09.033
Oh, I'm sorry. Hold on.

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:10.567
I'm getting word
that Patrick McHenry

00:05:10.567 --> 00:05:12.367
is back in the House chamber
right now.

00:05:12.367 --> 00:05:15.167
This is real. Can we go live
and see what he's up to?

00:05:18.834 --> 00:05:21.167
The chair welcomes everyone
to today's session.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:22.167
First order of business,

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.634
the chair recognizes
House Bill 3.817

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.667
to approve a short-term
spending bill.

00:05:26.667 --> 00:05:28.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.801 --> 00:05:33.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.801
Next, the chair recognizes
Bill 413.5

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.701
to make guacamole free
at all Chipotles.

00:05:44.701 --> 00:05:45.968
Ow!

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:47.467 --> 00:05:48.667
Yow!

00:05:52.467 --> 00:05:55.267
Next up, the chair declares
a new federal holiday --

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:57.033
Orville Redenbacher
Appreciation Day.

00:05:57.033 --> 00:05:58.901
Don't at me.

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.834
[ Applause ]

00:06:03.434 --> 00:06:05.467
Next, the chair
recognizes October 4th

00:06:05.467 --> 00:06:07.634
as the official start
of pumpkin spice season.

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.834
August is too early.
November is too late.

00:06:09.834 --> 00:06:11.868
It's settled.
Ow!

00:06:11.868 --> 00:06:14.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:18.300
Next item on the agenda,

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:20.601
the chair declares
Travis Kelce and Taylor Swift

00:06:20.601 --> 00:06:23.434
as the best couples Halloween
costume of the year.

00:06:23.434 --> 00:06:26.200
No one slay, slay like Tay-Tay.

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:28.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.934 --> 00:06:40.634
Pretty intense guy.

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:49.334
Pretty intense guy, like "Yow!"

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:51.100
Finally, officials in Australia

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:53.534
are warning people
to stay away from a swamp

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.934
that mysteriously
turned pink overnight.

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:57.067
Take a look at this thing.

00:06:57.067 --> 00:06:59.000
-Ooh.
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.801
-Turns out it was the world's
worst crocodile gender reveal.

